\[
\operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{b}} \mathbf{a} = \left( \frac{\mathbf{a} \cdot \mathbf{b}}{\mathbf{b} \cdot \mathbf{b}} \right) \mathbf{b}
\]
The numerator is the dot product of $\mathbf{a}$ and $\mathbf{b}$, which is $(3)(2) + (0)(-3) = 6$. The denominator is the dot product of $\mathbf{b}$ with itself, which is $(2)^2 + (-3)^2 = 13$. Therefore,
\begin{align*}
\operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{b}} \mathbf{a} &= \left( \frac{6}{13} \right) \begin{pmatrix} 2 \\ -3 \end{pmatrix} \\
&= \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} \frac{12}{13} \\ -\frac{18}{13} \end{pmatrix}}
